  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Moldova - &#x2018;Breaking the Cycle&#x2019; &#x2013; UNFPA-UNICEF Joint Project for Ending Violence Against Women and Children</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the United Nations Children&apos;s Fund (UNICEF) to reduce the prevalence of violence against women and children from Ukrainian refugee and Moldovan host communities through an integrated, multi-sectoral approach. The project strengthens national systems and community-based mechanisms to prevent and respond to gender-based violence (GBV) and violence against children (VAC), while promoting gender equality, social inclusion, and digital safety. It supports the implementation of the National Programme for Preventing and Combating Violence Against Women and Girls and Domestic Violence (2023&#x2013;2027), the National Program of Child Protection (2022&#x2013;2026), and the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection&#x2019;s RESTART reform.</narrative>
  </description>
